{{!-- The tab strip both actor sheets wear. For a character it carries Gold (`showGold`), because
      Gold is the number that changes most in play and it belongs beside the things it buys — and
      past the petty threshold it occupies slots, so the inventory below has to account for it
      anyway. An NPC has no purse in 2e (the Marketplace prices a hireling per day), so its strip
      ends at the last tab. The active tab wears a brush
      slab; Gold wears a drawn box; the rule under the strip is drawn, not a border. All of them,
      like every other mark on the sheet, are inked by `module/ink.js` from the element's measured
      size.

      Each slab is seeded by its own tab id rather than sharing one key. Only one is ever inked at
      a time, so they are never seen together — but a seed that changes with the tab means moving
      between them moves the brush mark too, instead of stamping the identical silhouette in a new
      place. --}}
<div class="cairn-tab-block">
    <nav class="tabs cairn-tab-strip" data-group="primary">
        {{#each tabs as |tab|}}
        {{!-- The slab sits INSIDE the label, not in the tab. Core stretches every tab in the strip
              to the same width, so a slab measured from the tab box is the width of the longest
              label whatever this one says — a mark around ORIGIN the width of INVENTORY.
              Measured from the label it hugs the word it is marking. --}}
        <a class="cairn-tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-action="tab" data-group="primary" data-tab="{{tab.id}}">
            <span>{{localize tab.label}}<span class="cairn-slab" data-ink="slab" data-ink-seed="tab-{{tab.id}}"></span></span>
        </a>
        {{/each}}

        {{#if showGold}}
        {{!-- Gold wears the chip treatment, not a brush slab. It sits at the far right of the
              strip on its own, with no upright between it and the last tab: the chip's drawn box
              already separates it from a row of bare capitals, and a second vertical mark 10px
              from it was one rule doing a job the box had done. A solid black mark this far down the
              page, with a field cut into it, read as a blot rather than as a control — and it was
              the only thing on the sheet drawn that way. An outlined box on paper puts it in the
              same family as Panicked and Rest, which is what it is: a thing on the sheet you can
              set. The label and the number share a BASELINE inside `.cairn-gold-pair`, and that
              pair is what the chip centres — a fixed-height box centring two different type sizes
              directly leaves the number sitting off the word's feet. --}}
        <label class="cairn-chip cairn-gold" data-ink="box" data-ink-seed="gold" data-ink-w="1.6">
            <span class="cairn-gold-pair">
                <span class="cairn-gold-label">{{localize 'CAIRN.Gold'}}</span>
                {{!-- Text, not number, so `maxlength` applies; digits are enforced as it is typed
                      by `actor-sheet.js#_attachPartListeners`. No `name`: `system.gold` is DERIVED — the sum
                      of the character's coin sacks (`data/item-coin.js`) — so the form must never
                      submit it. The chip's `change` turns the typed number into a difference and
                      moves that much coin (`module/coin.js#adjustGold`). --}}
                <input class="cairn-digits cairn-gold-input" type="text" value="{{system.gold}}"
                    maxlength="5" inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" />
            </span>
        </label>
        {{/if}}
    </nav>
    <div class="cairn-tab-rule" data-ink="hline" data-ink-seed="tab-rule" data-ink-w="1.8"></div>
</div>
